---
import ExampleSource from '../../components/ExampleSource.astro';
import Sample from '../../examples/arrange/app';
import Layout from '../../layouts/Layout.astro';
import { samplesSource } from '../../lib/links';
import { sitePath } from '../../lib/site-path';
import modelSource from '@opsydyn/effect-three-samples/src/arrange/model.ts?raw';
import messageSource from '@opsydyn/effect-three-samples/src/arrange/message.ts?raw';
import updateSource from '@opsydyn/effect-three-samples/src/arrange/update.ts?raw';
import sceneSource from '@opsydyn/effect-three-samples/src/arrange/scene.ts?raw';
import viewSource from '@opsydyn/effect-three-samples/src/arrange/view.ts?raw';
const sources = [{ name: 'model.ts', content: modelSource }, { name: 'message.ts', content: messageSource }, { name: 'update.ts', content: updateSource }, { name: 'scene.ts', content: sceneSource }, { name: 'view.ts', content: viewSource }];
---
<Layout title="Arrange — effect-three">
  <section class="page-intro"><a class="text-link" href={sitePath('/examples/')}>← All examples</a><p class="eyebrow">EDITING</p><h1>Move, turn, scale, undo.</h1><p>Click something on the table and a transform gizmo appears on it: drag an arrow to move it along an axis, a square to move it in a plane, a ring to turn it, or switch to scale. Shift-drag across empty space to box several things, and the gizmo moves them all alike. Press an axis in the corner to look along it, or switch to Drei-style pivot controls, every handle at once. Snap to quarter units and fifteen degrees, work in the object's own axes, and undo or redo every move. Drag empty space to orbit.</p></section>
  <Sample client:load noMeta />
  <noscript><p>This example needs JavaScript and WebGL to render the scene.</p></noscript>
  <section class="closing-callout"><h2>A gizmo as a Foldkit submodel.</h2><p>three's <code>TransformControls</code> listen to the canvas and move the object themselves. Here the gizmo's handles are scene nodes, a press and the drag rays after it are Messages, and each move comes back to the page as an OutMessage. The maths is three's, checked against its controls to six decimal places; the Model keeps every placement, so undo is a list. The selection box is a second submodel, after three's <code>SelectionBox</code>, and the axes in the corner a third, after Drei's <code>GizmoHelper</code>, drawn in the scene's HUD.</p><a class="text-link" href={samplesSource + '/arrange'}>Explore the example source →</a></section>
  <ExampleSource files={sources} />
</Layout>
